The hardest concept for me so far has been keeping track of how rotational motion connects back to the linear ideas we learned previously. Moment of intertia, torque, angular velocity, and angular momentum all make sense by themselves, but it definetly took some time for me to see how they work together in a simulation. 

However, something that did click this week was in realizing how similar the rotational equations are to the linear ones. Once I was able to wrap my head around torque as the rotational version of force and the moment of inertia as the rotational version of mass, it was very easy to move forward. In this way, the code became significantly easier to write and I began visualizing the simulation as I worked through it. 

Excited for the block 2 project!
